# Working memory

Agents update this file. It is the living snapshot of the project.

## Status

- **Status:** active
- **Updated:** 2026-10-24

## Project

- **Name:** Skyrope (codename; rename via search-replace `skyrope`)
- **Purpose:** 2D side-scrolling action MMORPG. Server-authoritative from day one. Inspired by classic 2000s Korean side-scrollers; original art, names, and world.
- **Owner:** Chris O'Neal
- **GitHub:** https://github.com/icors2/Action-Story (canonical remote; public; default branch `main`)
- **Stack:** Godot **4.7.2-stable** + typed GDScript (client + dedicated server, one project in `game/`). Python 3.12 + FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2 + Alembic + asyncpg (account/backend, Phase 11). PostgreSQL 16+ (Phase 11). GUT for Godot tests. pytest for backend.
- **Package manager:** Make at repo root. `uv` for backend (Phase 11). npm scripts only for Cursor layout audit.
- **Deploy target:** Docker Compose on a Linux homelab, Tailscale-only until Phase 16. Later: VPS.

## Current focus

- **Phase 2 complete. Stopped for play-test.** Default map is `map_test_movement` with 2 Puddlets + 1 Capshroom.
- LOCAL: walk/jump/climb + Ctrl/J attack, contact damage, death/respawn. No loot/EXP yet.
- Do not start Phase 3 until Chris play-tests combat.
- Next phase: **3 — RPG systems** (`implement-skyrope-phase`).
- Source of truth: `BUILD_SCOPE.md`. One phase at a time.

